 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500

@DISTRO_ID@-desktop (@OMARCHY_VERSION@+git20261014.22.8a7a6b3a-0@DISTRO_ID@1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * @DISTRO_ID@-desktop depends on localsend, as Omarchy preinstalls it:
    the Share menu and Files' "Send via LocalSend" have it to call. The
    package comes from this distro's repository (packages/localsend).
  * LocalSend's window rule and Files' "Send via LocalSend" extension are
    back; @DISTRO_ID@-config seeds the extension for new users and the
    port's first migration copies it for existing ones.
  * yt-dlp is back in the package list, with the native messaging host
    Chromium's Download Video extension calls; the migration registers
    the host for an existing user who has Chromium.
  * d/rules: copy migrations/ into the renamed tree, so the port's
    migrations reach the package (none was shipped before this one).

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0500

@DISTRO_ID@-desktop (@OMARCHY_VERSION@+git20261014.20.0559194c-0@DISTRO_ID@1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * Upstream version +git<date>.<count>.<commit> instead of +git<date>:
    the fork's commit count since the Omarchy tag orders several fork
    changes in one day, and the hash names the commit. Same fork commit
    as 4.0.4+git20261014-0@DISTRO_ID@1.
  * @DISTRO_ID@-config installs /etc/chromium.d/zz-@DISTRO_ID@-user-flags,
    which makes the Debian Chromium launcher read the user's
    ~/.config/chromium-flags.conf, as Arch's wrapper does: Omarchy's flags
    and its three bundled extensions now apply to Chromium.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:45:00 -0500

@DISTRO_ID@-desktop (@OMARCHY_VERSION@+git20261014-0@DISTRO_ID@1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * Install > Development installs build-essential (and unzip for OCaml)
    before building a toolchain: the image has no compiler.
  * Agents and mise tools from npm install Node.js first: the image has
    no Node.js.
  * Web apps use the first installed Chromium-based browser, and show a
    notification naming Install > Browser when there is none.
  * Steam and Lutris install the 32-bit Mesa and NVIDIA graphics drivers
    through the new hidden @DISTRO_ID@-install-32bit-graphics, since apt
    here installs no Recommends.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:30:00 -0500

@DISTRO_ID@-desktop (@OMARCHY_VERSION@+git20261013-0@DISTRO_ID@2) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * @DISTRO_ID@-desktop depends on ffmpegthumbnailer, so Files shows video
    thumbnails out of the box; it moved from the optional
    @DISTRO_ID@-desktop-apps, which keeps evince and gnome-disk-utility.
